There is an instructive ordinary analogue. Let multiplication by $x$ and differentiation by $x$ act on an arbitrary function $g(x)$. Then $\begin{aligned}
\partial_x\!\left(xg\right)&=g+xg',\\
x\partial_xg&=xg',\end{aligned}$ so $g=g.$ Because this holds for every $g$, $=1.$ With $p=-i\partial_x$, this is the familiar position-momentum algebra, in units with $\hbar=1$.

