The graded analogue of finding a Lie algebra is to compute $\begin{aligned}
\{Q,\bar Q\}
&=Q\bar Q+\bar Q Q\\
&=m\left(a_+c_-a_-c_+
        +a_-c_+a_+c_-\right).\end{aligned}$ Since the $a$’s are even, they pass through the $c$’s without a sign: $\{Q,\bar Q\}
=m\left(a_+a_-c_-c_+
        +a_-a_+c_+c_-\right).$ Now use $c_-c_+=1-c_+c_-,
\qquad
a_-a_+=a_+a_-+1.$ Then $\begin{aligned}
\{Q,\bar Q\}
&=m\left[
N_B(1-N_F)+(N_B+1)N_F
\right]\\
&=m(N_B+N_F).\end{aligned}$ The temporary extra factor of two that arose during the live rearrangement disappears: one contribution supplies $N_B$, the other supplies $N_F$.

